## 💡 Simple Example: What Is “Hawking Radiation”? 

Imagine a black hole isn’t completely “black”—it actually emits a faint, tiny glow of particles, theoretically allowing it to lose mass and (very slowly) shrink over time.  
_Physics takeaway:_ Even the most mysterious parts of our universe aren’t totally closed systems—information can “leak out” in unexpected ways.

